{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1708340,
  "courseSlug": "learn-flutter-dart-to-build-ios-android-apps",
  "courseTitle": "Flutter & Dart - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37145102",
      "title": "Finetuning Explicit Animations",
      "lectureOrder": 203,
      "videoOrder": 187,
      "sourceHash": "e86628c2b0ffc089e1111769f88a583fded8e2f28c8960987bbdb062a7e843f2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 4.154,
          "en": "Now, this animation here works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.154,
          "end": 7.25,
          "en": "and doesn't look too bad, but we can also build it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.25,
          "end": 12.06,
          "en": "in a slightly different and typically better way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.06,
          "end": 15.84,
          "en": "Instead of animating our padding like this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.84,
          "end": 20.25,
          "en": "we can also return a different value here in our builder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.25,
          "end": 23.97,
          "en": "We can return a slide transition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.97,
          "end": 28.44,
          "en": "And indeed, Flutter has many transition widgets built in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 28.44,
          "end": 29.94,
          "en": "If you take a look here for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.94,
          "end": 33.81,
          "en": "also have a FadeTransition, you have a SizeTransition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.81,
          "end": 36.96,
          "en": "to animate between two sizes for a widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.96,
          "end": 41.96,
          "en": "And AlignTransition to animate the position of a widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.06,
          "end": 46.26,
          "en": "A ScaleTransition to scale a widget up or down,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.26,
          "end": 50.76,
          "en": "or for example, a SlideTransition to animate the movement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 50.76,
          "end": 54.783,
          "en": "of a widget from one position to another, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 56.04,
          "end": 60.81,
          "en": "And for that, SlideTransition needs multiple parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 60.81,
          "end": 64.29,
          "en": "For example, it needs the child that should be animated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 64.29,
          "end": 66.318,
          "en": "In this case, it's still this child,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 66.318,
          "end": 69.78,
          "en": "which we're outsourcing here, the grid view,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 69.78,
          "end": 74.52,
          "en": "so that this grid view is not unnecessarily reevaluated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 74.52,
          "end": 76.95,
          "en": "But that's the child that will be animated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 76.95,
          "end": 79.68,
          "en": "by slight transition in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 79.68,
          "end": 81.423,
          "en": "Now, position also must be set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 81.423,
          "end": 83.67,
          "en": "and that's actually not a number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 83.67,
          "end": 88.67,
          "en": "but instead an animation that animates an offset.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 88.71000000000001,
          "end": 90.24,
          "en": "Now, what's that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.24,
          "end": 92.37899999999999,
          "en": "Now, an animation in the end is what we get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.37899999999999,
          "end": 95.1,
          "en": "with help of animationController.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 95.1,
          "end": 97.5,
          "en": "That's an animation in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.5,
          "end": 100.8,
          "en": "And offset then is a special kind of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.8,
          "end": 103.369,
          "en": "used by Flutter to describe the,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.369,
          "end": 107.22,
          "en": "well, amount of offset of an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.22,
          "end": 111.27000000000001,
          "en": "from the actual position it would normally take.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 111.27000000000001,
          "end": 112.95,
          "en": "And to make this a bit clearer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.95,
          "end": 115.86,
          "en": "let's simply start adding a value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.86,
          "end": 119.7,
          "en": "And the animation I will add is my animation controller.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.7,
          "end": 120.8,
          "en": "And on that controller,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.8,
          "end": 124.71,
          "en": "you can call the built-in drive method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.71,
          "end": 126.39,
          "en": "Now, this simply is a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.39,
          "end": 130.47,
          "en": "that can be used to build an animation, as you can see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.47,
          "end": 132.84,
          "en": "based on some other value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.84,
          "end": 135.39,
          "en": "So in the end, it is a method that can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.39,
          "end": 139.68,
          "en": "to translate this animation between these two values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.68,
          "end": 142.07999999999998,
          "en": "zero and 1 to an animation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.07999999999998,
          "end": 146.01,
          "en": "between two other kinds of values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.01,
          "end": 148.237,
          "en": "For example, between two offsets here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.237,
          "end": 151.277,
          "en": "because here we need an animation over offsets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.277,
          "end": 154.53,
          "en": "not an animation between two doubles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.53,
          "end": 157.293,
          "en": "Not an animation between zero and 1.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.28,
          "end": 161.94,
          "en": "And drive simply allows us to translate our animation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 161.94,
          "end": 164.57999999999998,
          "en": "between zero and 1 to an animation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.57999999999998,
          "end": 166.71,
          "en": "between two other values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.71,
          "end": 170.91,
          "en": "For that, drive wants an animatable child.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.91,
          "end": 173.85,
          "en": "And such a animatable child can be built",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.85,
          "end": 177.9,
          "en": "with Flutter's Tween class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.9,
          "end": 180.372,
          "en": "The Tween class creates tween objects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.372,
          "end": 183.93,
          "en": "and the name tween simply comes from the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183.93,
          "end": 188.69,
          "en": "that this class and these objects are all about animating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.69,
          "end": 192.96,
          "en": "or describing the transition between,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 192.96,
          "end": 196.713,
          "en": "hence the name tween, two values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.97,
          "end": 200.73,
          "en": "And for that tween takes two values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.73,
          "end": 203.613,
          "en": "as you might guess, begin and end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.93,
          "end": 207.627,
          "en": "And now, here we wanna animate between two offsets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.627,
          "end": 212.627,
          "en": "because position wants an animation over offset values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 214.05,
          "end": 219.05,
          "en": "Such a offset can be created with Flutter's Offset class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 219.42000000000002,
          "end": 222.801,
          "en": "And Offset simply takes two doubles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 222.801,
          "end": 226.82999999999998,
          "en": "two numbers with decimal places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 226.82999999999998,
          "end": 230.16,
          "en": "The first number describes the offset on the X axis",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 230.16,
          "end": 232.98,
          "en": "and the second number on the Y axis.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 232.98,
          "end": 236.7,
          "en": "So, here where we're talking about sliding some element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 236.7,
          "end": 239.361,
          "en": "we're basically saying how much to the right",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 239.361,
          "end": 242.737,
          "en": "or left on the X axis and how much to the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 242.737,
          "end": 246.51,
          "en": "or bottom on the Y axis should we start?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 246.51,
          "end": 249.532,
          "en": "And here you can enter values for both X and Y,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 249.532,
          "end": 252.81,
          "en": "between zero and 1.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 252.81,
          "end": 255.63,
          "en": "And zero simply means that there is no offset.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 255.63,
          "end": 259.773,
          "en": "And 1 means that there is an offset by 100% in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 260.7,
          "end": 264.81,
          "en": "And here I want no offset on the X axis initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 264.81,
          "end": 269.81,
          "en": "but I want some offset, let's say 30% offset on the Y axis,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 270.51,
          "end": 274.5,
          "en": "so that the content is pushed 30% down.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 274.5,
          "end": 276.57,
          "en": "And this can be a const value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 276.57,
          "end": 278.67,
          "en": "because even though we're going to animate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 278.67,
          "end": 281.4,
          "en": "the starting point is constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 281.4,
          "end": 284.25,
          "en": "And the same is true for the endpoint.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 284.25,
          "end": 287.07,
          "en": "And here I want to have an offset of 0, 0",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 287.07,
          "end": 289.487,
          "en": "because I wanna end at the actual position",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 289.487,
          "end": 292.233,
          "en": "my grid view would normally have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 293.67,
          "end": 295.182,
          "en": "So, now these are the two values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 295.182,
          "end": 297.51,
          "en": "between which we wanna animate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 297.51,
          "end": 300.93,
          "en": "And now, Flutter will figure out how to translate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 300.93,
          "end": 303.393,
          "en": "this animation between zero and 1",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 303.393,
          "end": 307.118,
          "en": "to this translation between these two values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 307.118,
          "end": 310.983,
          "en": "That is what drive does in conjunction with Tween.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 312.3,
          "end": 315.368,
          "en": "And with that, if we now save this and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 315.368,
          "end": 318.45,
          "en": "we will see that we again get a sliding animation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 318.45,
          "end": 322.53,
          "en": "But now actually, thanks to us using SlideTransition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 322.53,
          "end": 326.85,
          "en": "this animation behind the scenes is a bit more optimized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 326.85,
          "end": 331.85,
          "en": "and it also gives us some extra features and capabilities.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 332.13,
          "end": 334.047,
          "en": "So, which extra features do we get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 334.047,
          "end": 337.413,
          "en": "by using this way of animating the SlideTransition?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 338.52,
          "end": 343.14,
          "en": "Well, on this Tween, we can call the animate method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 343.14,
          "end": 346.293,
          "en": "and animate all the returns and animation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 347.19,
          "end": 351.3,
          "en": "Therefore, we can indeed replace animationController.drive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 351.3,
          "end": 356.3,
          "en": "with Tween animate since animate returns such a animation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 356.97,
          "end": 361.47,
          "en": "over an offset, which is exactly what position wants.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 361.47,
          "end": 364.11,
          "en": "But now, animate takes an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 364.11,
          "end": 366.909,
          "en": "which we can use to get more control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 366.909,
          "end": 371.31,
          "en": "over how the animation is played back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 371.31,
          "end": 375.15,
          "en": "To be precise, we can pass in a CurvedAnimation here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 375.15,
          "end": 377.52,
          "en": "Another object created with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 377.52,
          "end": 380.043,
          "en": "of another class provided by Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 381.42,
          "end": 385.17,
          "en": "Now, CurvedAnimation in the end is a configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 385.17,
          "end": 387.63,
          "en": "for creating such animation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 387.63,
          "end": 389.943,
          "en": "with help of this animate method here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 391.02,
          "end": 393.9,
          "en": "CurvedAnimation then takes a parent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 393.9,
          "end": 396.57,
          "en": "which is nothing else than our animationController.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 396.57,
          "end": 399.273,
          "en": "So, the thing that controls the animation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 400.11,
          "end": 402.6,
          "en": "And it then takes a curve.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 402.6,
          "end": 405.116,
          "en": "And the curve here wants a curve value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 405.116,
          "end": 406.32,
          "en": "But no worries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 406.32,
          "end": 408.96,
          "en": "Here, you don't have to create one yourselves.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 408.96,
          "end": 413.46,
          "en": "Instead, there is a Curves object or a Curves class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 413.46,
          "end": 415.02,
          "en": "built into Flutter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 415.02,
          "end": 418.74,
          "en": "with a bunch of predefined animation curves.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 418.74,
          "end": 422.716,
          "en": "And these curves simply control how the transition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 422.716,
          "end": 427.068,
          "en": "between the begin and end state will be spread",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 427.068,
          "end": 430.533,
          "en": "over the available animation time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 431.46,
          "end": 434.75,
          "en": "So that we, for example, don't have a linear animation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 434.75,
          "end": 439.75,
          "en": "but one where we start slow and end slow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 439.98,
          "end": 443.61,
          "en": "so that we have some acceleration in the middle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 443.61,
          "end": 447.87,
          "en": "but we end smoothly and start smoothly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 447.87,
          "end": 450.96,
          "en": "And you can simply play around with these different curves",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 450.96,
          "end": 454.473,
          "en": "to give your animations a more natural feel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 455.85,
          "end": 457.98,
          "en": "That's the idea behind setting curves.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
